 Before a full QA review, the app decides without a model where the project's full suite runs: on this machine, on the forge's CI from the task's branch pushed without a PR (GitHub Actions, Azure Pipelines, GitLab CI, Bitbucket Pipelines, Jenkins), or on the WorkPilot server, from the free CPU, RAM, GPU and VRAM and the suite's measured load; with no room, the suite queues, it is never skipped. The touched tests run first, a card's own choice wins over the project's, the merge waits while the CI runs, and after a merge the other green cards take the new base and run again. Design: [test-placement.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/test-placement.md), [suite-base-refresh.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/suite-base-refresh.md).
 
+### Resuming after a close or a crash
+
+Closing WorkPilot pauses the builds that run (the Pause button's own pause, in every spec copy), and the next launch asks which to resume. Each build shows its project, its provider and model, how it stopped (WorkPilot closed, WorkPilot stopped without closing, or « Stop all agents ») and where it picks up: Spec, Plan, Code n/m with the next subtask, or QA.
+
+- **Ticked by default**: what the app interrupted. A « Stop all agents » or voice « stop » is listed unticked, and a build whose resume would fail at once (Claude sign-in expired for a build on Claude, spec folder gone) is unticked with the reason and a « Reconnect » link.
+- **In Progress limit**: each project's limit is kept; past it, a build waits and starts when a slot frees up.
+- **Later** (or Escape): the builds stay paused and are not offered at the next launch. Their card reads **Interrupted**, with how and when in its tooltip, and a Resume button; a paused card is never read as « Stuck », so the stuck recovery never resets the subtask it stopped on. The toolbar's « N interrupted tasks · Resume… » brings the list back.
+- **Settings > Agent Settings**: Ask me (default), Resume all (what the app interrupted, without your own stops) or Resume none. « Next time » in the dialog saves the same choice.
+
+Every resume takes the Resume button's path: the backend re-enters the phase from the spec folder, continues the subtask the build was on and reopens the Claude session when there is one, on every provider. Design: [pause-resume.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/pause-resume.md).
+
 ### Actions available on a card
 
 - **Preview** (screen icon) — launches the app in the embedded **App Emulator**
